  "testers": [],
  "findings": [
    {
      "text": "Magistral Medium was trained with pure reinforcement learning (RL) on Mistral Medium 3 (no distillation), with about a 50% AIME-24 pass@1 gain over the starting checkpoint.", "tone": "mixed",
      "source": {
        "page": "2",
        "pdfPage": 2,
        "quote": "strength of our proposed RLVR framework, which yields a 50% increase in AIME-24 (pass@1) over the initial"
      }
    },
    {
      "text": "Unlike prior DeepSeek-R1 findings, RL on the smaller 24B model still beat distillation-only, and supervised fine-tuning (SFT)+RL was best for Magistral Small.", "tone": "neutral",
      "source": {
        "page": "9",
        "pdfPage": 9,
        "quote": "Here, contrary to findings"
      }
    },
    {
      "text": "Text-only RL did not erase multimodal ability; the paper reports gains on [MMMU](https://arxiv.org/abs/2311.16502) and MMMU-Pro after RL.", "tone": "mixed",
      "source": {
        "page": "14",
        "pdfPage": 14,
        "quote": "contrary, we discover that the models not only retain their multimodal capabilities, but unexpectedly"
      }
    },
    {
      "text": "A language-consistency reward plus translated math problems is used so chain-of-thought and the answer match the user’s language.", "tone": "neutral",
      "source": {
        "page": "4",
        "pdfPage": 4,
        "quote": "A core design principle for Magistral is for it to reason in the same language as the user. Reinforcement"
      }
    },
    {
      "text": "On multilingual AIME’24, Magistral Medium scores 4.3–9.9% lower than English (about 1–3 questions).", "tone": "neutral",
      "source": {
        "page": "9",
        "pdfPage": 9,
        "quote": "performs 4.3-9.9% lower on multilingual versions compared to English, which corresponds to 1-3"
      }
    },
    {
      "text": "An alternate Medium path (SFT on open-source R1 traces, then RL) reaches R1-like math/code scores; [GPQA](https://arxiv.org/abs/2311.12022) Diamond fell from 72.9% to 71.0% after that RL.", "tone": "mixed",
      "source": {
        "page": "16",
        "pdfPage": 16,
        "quote": "Please note that the performance on GPQA Diamond drops after RL from 72.9% to 71.0%."
      }
    }
  ],
